      "title": "The concern changes from early death to long life",
      "narration": "Rosa and David are approaching retirement. They already understand life insurance as protection against the financial consequences of a covered death. Now they ask how to create income if they live much longer than expected. An annuity is a contract with an insurance company that can provide payments immediately or at a later time. A lifetime income option addresses longevity risk: the risk of outliving income resources. Not every annuity payment option lasts for life. A fixed period of payments can end while the recipient is still living. Identify the promised income pattern before assuming that every annuity eliminates that risk.",
