      "title": "Accumulation is the stage before income conversion",
      "narration": "During a deferred annuity's accumulation phase, the contract holds value under its crediting or investment provisions. Rosa may fund a contract with one premium or a permitted series of premiums. The value can change with interest, investment performance, charges and withdrawals, depending on the design. Accumulation does not mean all annuities earn the same guaranteed rate. It also does not mean money is freely accessible without consequences. A withdrawal can involve surrender charges, adjustments and tax effects. Track the contract value and the amount available on surrender separately. The accumulation stage describes where the contract is in its operation, not which investment guarantees it contains.",
