      "narration": "Annuitization converts the applicable value into a series of payments under the selected settlement option. The option determines whether income lasts for one life, two lives or a stated period, and whether anything continues after a death. This decision often limits access to the amount converted and can be difficult or impossible to reverse under the contract. A monthly withdrawal from an account is not automatically annuitization. Some optional lifetime-withdrawal benefits operate differently from converting the contract into annuity payments. For this lesson, separate accumulating value, taking a withdrawal and formally choosing an annuity income option. The next lessons compare the payment patterns in detail.",
